==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is an [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]].
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*1 [[Otta-smack-u]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*2 [[Pigge]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Cerberus Kids]] spawns as the boss.
**4 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
**10 [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
**2 [[Otta-smack-u]]s spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
**5 [[Pigge]]s spawn, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is optimized for level 9 units. If you struggle, it may be worth waiting for earlier stages to become available and clearing those first. Having said this, this stage grants plenty of time to prepare and doesn't contain strong pushers, meaning that you can easily beat this stage even with level 2 cats. For this reason, tackling this stage early is likely to bring benefit.

Bring a trio of cats with a cost of 75¢, [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]], [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon Cat]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] and [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]]. Start when the first enemies get close with Crazed Dragon and one-two meatshields until you get the [[Worker Cat]] to level 3, then add Bahamut and spam. Once Bahamut dies, summon Ururun, and for the rest just spam to win. Keep in mind that the [[Cat Cannon|Cannon]]'s damage is still relevant at this point.

